<title>USA: James River to sell timberlands for $110 mln.</title>
<headline>James River to sell timberlands for $110 mln.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>James River Corp said Thursday it has signed a definitive agreement with the Hancock Timber Resource Group, an investment unit of John Hancock Mutual Life Insurance Co, of Boston, Mass., for the sale of about 95,000 acres of timberlands in Alabama and Mississippi.</p>
<p>James River said it will receive in excess of $110 million in cash, subject to normal closing adjustments.</p>
<p>The sale is expected to generate a gain and is scheduled to close in April, subject to normal closing conditions, the company said.</p>
</text>
